# What the Docker build is allowed to see.
#
# This file is a security control before it is a performance one. The build
# context is everything `docker build` uploads to the daemon, and anything in
# it can be baked into a layer by a single careless COPY -- including layers of
# an image somebody later pushes to a registry. The repository root holds a
# production database dump; without this file it would be in every build
# context, one `COPY . .` away from being published.
#
# Deny by default, then allow back only what the build needs. An exclusion list
# would have to anticipate every future secret; an allowlist only has to
# anticipate the build.
*

# The backend build: the wrapper, its build files, and the sources.
!backend/gradlew
!backend/gradle
!backend/settings.gradle
!backend/build.gradle
!backend/gradle.properties
!backend/src

# Never, even though `*` already excludes them -- these are the paths where
# being wrong is unrecoverable, so they are stated rather than inferred. A
# later `!backend/**` written in a hurry would otherwise silently re-admit
# whatever landed under an allowed prefix.
backend/build
backend/.gradle
**/*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/seed/*.sql
**/*.sql.gz
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
.git
